{"name":"True Blue","hex":"#010fcc","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"true blue","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Steadfastly faithful or loyal; unwavering in loyalty; staunch, true.","Patriotic."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A faithful partisan or supporter of a cause, person, political party, etc.","A blue dye from Coventry, England, famous for not washing out."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/true_blue"}],"entries":[{"title":"True Blue (album)","blocks":[{"text":"True Blue is the third studio album by American singer and songwriter Madonna. It was released on June 30, 1986, by Sire Records. Madonna had greater control over the creative direction of True Blue than on her second studio album, Like a Virgin (1984), as she attempted to establish herself as a serious artist and appeal to a broader, more mature audience."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/e/e0/Madonna_-_True_Blue_%28album_cover%29.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/True_Blue_(album)","wikidata":"Q154467"},{"title":"True Blue (Madonna song)","blocks":[{"text":"\"True Blue\" is a song by American singer Madonna from her third studio album of the same name (1986). Written and produced by the singer and her collaborator Stephen Bray, it was released to radio on September 13, 1986. In Australia, New Zealand, and most European countries, it was released as the album's third single in the USA on September 17th 1986. Physically released as a single in the United States on October 9. A dance-pop song that takes influence from Motown and girl groups from the 1950s and 1960s, \"True Blue\" addresses Madonna's feelings for her then-husband Sean Penn."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/2/2e/Madonna_-_True_Blue_%28single%29.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/True_Blue_(Madonna_song)","wikidata":"Q1509040"},{"title":"Blue","blocks":[{"text":"Blue is one of the three primary colours in the RGB (additive) colour model, as well as in the RYB colour model. It lies between violet and cyan on the spectrum of visible light. The term blue generally describes colours perceived by humans observing light with a dominant wavelength between approximately 450 and 495 nanometres. The clear daytime sky and the deep sea appear blue because of an optical effect known as Rayleigh scattering. An optical effect called the Tyndall effect explains blue eyes. Distant objects appear more blue because of another optical effect called aerial perspective."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5a/Earth-in-true-color-himawari-09.jpg/330px-Earth-in-true-color-himawari-09.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Blue","wikidata":"Q1088"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/63/James_cagney_promo_photo_%28cropped%2C_centered%29.jpg/500px-James_cagney_promo_photo_%28cropped%2C_centered%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/63/James_cagney_promo_photo_%28cropped%2C_centered%29.jpg/500px-James_cagney_promo_photo_%28cropped%2C_centered%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AJames_cagney_promo_photo_(cropped%2C_centered).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/ce/James_Dean_in_Rebel_Without_a_Cause_%28HQ%29.jpg/500px-James_Dean_in_Rebel_Without_a_Cause_%28HQ%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/ce/James_Dean_in_Rebel_Without_a_Cause_%28HQ%29.jpg/1280px-James_Dean_in_Rebel_Without_a_Cause_%28HQ%29.jp